# count_alloc_copy_idiom.tkr — the RM-C2 no-push idiom fixture (crumb 0020). `main.tks` counts
# the total length of three byte pieces, allocates `var final: [total]byte = []` once, and copies
# each piece into its exact offset via `teko::runtime::copy` — no `push`, no growth, one
# allocation. It exits 0 only if the assembled buffer matches the expected concatenation
# byte-for-byte and `final.len` equals the counted total. `src/` does not yet call `copy`, so this
# path is not fixpoint-exercised.

Feature: count_alloc_copy_idiom — count -> [total]byte=[] -> copy assembles a flat, non-growing buffer

  Scenario: three_pieces_copied_by_index_reassemble_byte_exact
    When the program is built and run
    Then it exits 0
